    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass and the build succeeds. The implementation is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a structured address form for owners while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**OpenAPI contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)\n- Added `addressLine1` and `addressLine2` properties to the `OwnerFields` schema (these generate the DTO fields used across the pipeline).\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list so a minimal/structured owner still validates \u2014 presence is now enforced in code so either form is accepted.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns to all four schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres; tests run on hsqldb) and the matching `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` JPA fields + getters/setters on the `Owner` entity so they round-trip through the DB and serialize in responses.\n\n**Address resolution** (`OwnerAddress.apply(request)`) \u2014 one shared authority that:\n- Prefers the structured fields when `addressLine1` is non-blank, normalizing `addressLine1` and (when present) `addressLine2`, then composes `address` = normalized `addressLine1` + a single space + normalized `addressLine2` (just `addressLine1` when line 2 is absent).\n- Falls back to normalizing the flat `address` otherwise.\n\n**Pipelines**\n- `ValidateNewOwner` (POST) calls `OwnerAddress.apply` up front, then its required-field check treats a blank composed `address` as \"address missing\" \u2014 so an owner is valid with either a non-blank `addressLine1` or a flat `address`, plus city. `BuildOwner` maps the normalized fields onto the entity via the existing MapStruct mapper.\n- `ValidateOwner` (PUT) applies the same normalization/composition.\n- `ApplyOwner` (PUT) now copies `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` onto the entity.\n\nThe household hash, postcode validation and locality continue to derive from `postcode`/`city`/`lastName`, which are shared by both address forms, so they operate correctly on the structured fields when present and on the flat form otherwise.\n\nI also added a test (`composesAddressLine2WhenPresent`) covering the previously-untested `addressLine2` composition branch. `mvn test` \u2192 **Tests run: 3, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\nOne behavioral note worth flagging: dropping `address` from the OpenAPI `required` list also relaxes the `@Valid`-enforced PUT path (a bodyless `address` is no longer rejected by schema validation there), which is the intended backward-compatible contract but is a real change to PUT.",
